# Important Design Principle

The system should **not treat the workflow as merely a list of approvers**.

The workflow should be a reusable process engine where each request gets a snapshot of the workflow that was active when the request was submitted.

This is important because workflows may change later.

For example:
 
Request #001
uses Workflow Version 2

Request #002
uses Workflow Version 3


Even if Version 3 becomes the current workflow, Request #001 must continue to use its original workflow snapshot.

This ensures historical requests remain accurate and auditable.
